# Plants

Separate layer. Do not retune human PD or 200 Hz. Play is scene `Tree`.
Keep `treeCount = 0` and `flowerCount = 0` in `SampleScene` and `World`
(`LevelGrove` is the yard picture, not `treeCount`).

The builder class is `PlantTree`, not `Tree`: Unity already has
`UnityEngine.Tree`. A segment is `HumanSegment` (box + Visual), same as
the bird. Size is `collider.size`, not `localScale`. Leaves are
`InitializeVisualOnly`, no rigidbody.

## Two rigs

| `TreeRig` | Where | Bodies |
|---|---|---|
| `Sway` | scene `Tree`, headless `-tree 1` | static stump + up to 15 dynamic hinges |
| `Static` | yard grove, Tree-scene extras | **picture only**: no `Rigidbody2D`, no wood collider |

Static **Apple** (Level1 `YardApple`) look-sways the picture in
`LateUpdate`: wind plus the same fly-by unit as `ApplyBirdWake`.
Wood transforms and `BirdPerch` pads stay at the grow pose, so Ground
colliders are not dragged. Do not promote that apple to `Sway` — one
Human of hinges next to the Level1 flock is too dear. World grove
kinds (oak…poplar) stay frozen.

One `Sway` tree costs about one `Human` in body count. Do not plant a
`Sway` grove in `World`.

Static is for hundreds of plants. A segment is still a box sprite
(`HumanSegment.size`, not `localScale`). It does not enter Box2D.
Sit contact is only `BirdPerch` pads (Ground, no extra RB, cap 20,
twigs first). Wood vs world / human / bird is off because there is
no wood fixture. `GetPerchSlots` / `SeatBirds` / `NearPerch` stay.
Sway keep the old 31-body clamp; Static may grow to 255 segments.

## Recursion

`Grow` from the parent's tip: a leader near the axis, a side branch at
`forkAngle`. Side alternates so CoM stays over the stump.
`maxDepth = 3` → up to 15 segments. `maxSegments` cuts growth.

`TreeKind` picks the recipe. **Oak** is the hold/perch canon (same
numbers as 30.08). Pine is tall and sparse, willow wide (Sway weeps
a little), bush short with a three-way root, poplar thin.
**Apple** is opt-in (`ParseKind "apple"`, not in the yard 0…4 cycle):
3 m leader, wide fork, fruit sprites only. Sway uses the same hold
path and the Human-sized 15-body cap. Level1 plants it `Static` via
`LevelGrove`, not `treeCount`, and `PlantTree` look-sways that picture.
Static Apple grows a denser crown (depth 5, three-way forks on the
first two levels, cap 96 picture segments), fruit on outer twigs
(2–3 per twig), perch on wood tips and mid-span (pads cap 48). World
grove is not Apple.
Four Play-gallery kinds (not in the yard cycle): **Lilac** (green
Y-stem, purple ellipse blooms), **Hazel** (three trunks, catkin
ellipses), **Cedar** (layered near-horizontal fans), **Plum** (square
fruit clusters). Sway stays inside the 31-body cap; Static may grow
deeper (depth 4–6). Look-sway is Apple + those four. Oak…Poplar
Static stay frozen (World grove).
`KindFromPlantIndex` cycles 0…4 (yard grove). `KindFromGalleryIndex`
is Oak…Poplar then Lilac Hazel Cedar Plum. Scene `Tree` plants nine
(first `Sway`, rest `Static`). Headless default is oak; `-treeKind
pine` / `-treeKind apple` / `-treeKind lilac`.
Do not plant a `Sway` row in `World`.

## Hold pose, still bend

Wood gravity is cancelled at the grow pose (`TreeSpring.holdTorque`).
Without that, a side branch sags to the hinge limit — it looks like the
branch fell off. Extra mass (a bird on `Ground`) is not in the hold
sum, so `stiffness` still bends the joint. Apple Sway also applies
`worldStiffness` on the trunk (stump is Static); forks stay on the
joint spring so a world error cannot yank the crown.

Human hinges: `+AddTorque` (CCW) **decreases** `jointAngle`. Wood spring
is `+k·(θ−θ_rest)`, not textbook `−k·θ`. Cap by `maxTorque` only —
a one-step `springStop` is < 1 N·m on wood inertia and kills the pose.

Sway wood colliders use the `Ground` layer; a bird does not collide
with them (`Bird.GhostTreeWood`). Static wood has no collider.
Sit points are `BirdPerch` pads from `EnsureBirdPerches` (oak: top of
twigs, cap 20; Apple: wood tip and mid-span, cap 48). `GetPerchSlots` /
`SeatBirds` / `NearPerch` stay the handshake with agent `ai`. Play flock:
`BirdFlock50` has `treeCount = 1` (Sway).
Headless: `-tree 1`, Static grove `-treeRig static`. With birds
`-bird 1 -tree 1`. Do not plant pads in World unless a bird is there.

Accepted 02.09 (`plant_static_cheap_02.md`): Static oak is 0 RB / 0
wood collider. Sway hold still ≈ 0.002°. One flock bird on Static
pads: `perchLandCount` 7, `fell` false.

Pass 03.09: Static build skips mass normalize, `SyncTransforms`, and
hold bind. Perch slots are collected once. Leaves are a sprite on the
twig, not a `HumanSegment`. Sway path is unchanged.

## Do not

- No muscles and no `HingeJoint2D.useMotor`. Wood is `TreeSpring` +
  `JointFriction`.
- Do not put a wood `Rigidbody2D` or wood collider back on Static.
- Forces only in `FixedUpdate` through `TreeDriver` (spring → damping →
  wind → bird wake). Look-sway of Static Apple is picture only
  (`LateUpdate`), not a force.
- Wind is `½ ρ v² S` on the segment, not an "up" force.
- A flying bird near a Sway branch adds a local horizontal gust
  (`ApplyBirdWake`). Wood is ghost to the bird, so there is no solver
  contact; the wake is the fly-by reaction. Sit / Walk / Static stay
  quiet on the solver. Static Apple still look-bends from the same
  fly-by unit (`lookBirdSwayDegrees`). No force on the bird. No Linecast.
  Not an "up" force.
- The stump is Static. The tree does not fall like a human ragdoll.
- Do not bake bark/leaf textures here: card `VIS-TREE`, do not change
  collider size.

## Garden flowers (not a tree)

Small plants are `PlantFlower`, not `PlantTree`. Twelve subclasses
lock `FlowerKind`: Rose, Tulip, Daisy, Poppy, Sunflower, Lily,
Daffodil, Violet, Crocus, Lavender, Iris, Bluebell.

Picture only: `HumanSegment.InitializeVisualOnly`. No `Rigidbody2D`,
no collider, no `TreeSpring`, no wind, no `BirdPerch`. A bird does
not sit on a bloom. Cost is sprites, not 15 bodies.

Stem is 9–42 cm (crocus … sunflower). Play gallery is scene `Tree`
(`flowerCount = 12`). World and `SampleScene` stay `flowerCount = 0`.
Headless: `-flower 1` (row of 12) or `-flower 1 -flowerKind rose`.
Do not plant a Sway grove of flowers. A yard bed is a later level
card, not this layer.
